Subject: mysqlnd: connect to "localhost" over TCP on OpenVMS

For the host name "localhost", mysqlnd connects through the Unix-domain
socket unix:///tmp/mysql.sock (or mysqli.default_socket).  OpenVMS has no
usable Unix-domain sockets for this, so mysqli_connect("localhost", ...)
failed at once with 2002 "Operation not permitted".  phpBB's installer
writes $dbhost = 'localhost' by default, and the board switched to this
PHP was down until its config.php said 127.0.0.1 (vms-php PORTING_LOG
#62).  On VMS, "localhost" now takes the TCP path, tcp://localhost:port,
as any other host name does.
---
--- a/ext/mysqlnd/mysqlnd_connection.c
+++ b/ext/mysqlnd/mysqlnd_connection.c
@@ -524,7 +524,13 @@
 {
 	MYSQLND_STRING transport;
 	DBG_ENTER("mysqlnd_conn_data::get_scheme");
-#ifndef PHP_WIN32
+#if defined(__VMS)
+	/* OpenVMS has no usable Unix-domain sockets for this: connecting to
+	 * "localhost" as unix:///tmp/mysql.sock fails at once with "Operation
+	 * not permitted" (2002), as phpBB's default dbhost does (vms-php
+	 * PORTING_LOG #62).  "localhost" takes the TCP path below. */
+	if (0) {
+#elif !defined(PHP_WIN32)
